{"name":"Just About White","hex":"#e8e8e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"just","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Factually right, correct; factual.","Rationally right, correct."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Only, simply, merely.","Introduces a disappointing or surprising outcome that renders futile something previously mentioned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just"},{"term":"about","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["In a circle around; all round; on every side of; on the outside of; around. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Over or upon different parts of; through or over in various directions; here and there in; to and fro in; throughout."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On all sides, or in every or any direction from a point; around.","Here and there; around; in one place and another; up and down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/De